# Sound handles are pointers, so they must be host width.
#
# The audio API returns a "voice id" that is really a SFXEmitter* cast to an
# integer, and the decomp types it as `unsigned long`. That is 32 bits in this
# build (Windows LLP64), so every handle returned by cGameSFX::Play and its
# overrides lost the top half of the address. Widened to std::uintptr_t across
# the virtual chain -- the base declaration and every override have to move
# together or the overrides stop overriding.
#
# Also here: plataudio GetSndIDError() returned 0, which is a plausible handle;
# it now returns (u32)-1, the value the Nis code already compares against.
# Nis index comparisons accept both the host-width and the old 32-bit -1.
